title: "Convex, symmetric and transitory: growing-season climate variability and food prices in 153 countries"
abstract: >-
  Replication package for a study of how growing-season climate variability transmits
  into domestic food prices across 153 countries, 2003-2025. The signed temperature
  anomaly conventionally used in the weather-and-prices literature is statistically
  indistinguishable from zero, while its square is not. The price response is convex
  in the anomaly, symmetric across the hot and cold tails, and exhausted within about
  eighteen months.

